    "NETPMD MERGER CREATES ACTIVE TOOL CONSOLIDATION PRESSURE: Centillion's own merger announcement acknowledges 'near-term integration complexity.' NetPMD is described as bringing 'project management and design tools and workflows for OSP design' — meaning Centillion now has two overlapping design toolsets post-merger. This is a classic consolidation moment where a third-party tool like Inorsa can be positioned as a clean, neutral layer above both legacy stacks rather than requiring either to be chosen. Source: centillionsolutions.com/centillion-solutions-expands-capabilities-with-netpmd-solutions-merger/",
    "8,000 EMPLOYEES — SCALE DISCREPANCY REQUIRES CLARIFICATION: AE booth notes state '~8,000 employees, a number of those based in India.' LinkedIn shows only 267 followers and the company was founded in 2021. ZoomInfo suggests a much smaller firm. The 8,000 number may refer to a parent entity, holding company, or affiliated staffing network rather than Centillion Solutions itself. CEO Murali Nair's LinkedIn profile references India-based operations, which is consistent with AE notes. Source: AE booth notes, linkedin.com/company/centillion-solutions, zoominfo.com/c/centillion-solutions/547613817, linkedin.com/in/murali-nair",
